<quiz><question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Assessing Product Success: Probability Analysis and Review Evaluation</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Customers are used to evaluate preliminary product designs. In the past  \({@A@} \%\) of highly successful products recived good reviews \(, {@B@} \%\) of moderately successful products recived good reviews, and \({@C@} \%\) of poor products recived good reviews. In addition, \({@product_A@}\% \) of the products have been highly successful \(, {@product_B@}\%\) have been moderately successful and \({@product_C@}\%\) have been poor products. 
<p><b>Note:</b> Give your answer to 3 decimal places.</p>
<p>a) What is the probability that a product attain good review?</p>
<p>\(P(G)=\)[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>b) If a new design attain a good review, what is the probability that it will be a highly successful product?</p>
<p>\(P(H|G)=\)[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]][[feedback:prt2]]</p>
<p>c)  If a product does not attain a good review, what is the probability that it will be highly successful?
<p>\(P(H|G^{\prime})=\)[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]][[feedback:prt3]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>

<p>a)  \(P(G)=P(H)P(G|H)+P(M)P(G|M)+P(P)P(G|P)\)</p>
<p> \(P(G)=({@prob_A@} \times {@product_A_1@})+({@prob_B@} \times {@product_B_1@})+({@prob_C@} \times {@product_C_1@})\)</p>
<p> \(P(G)={@ta_1@}\)</p>
<p>b) \(\displaystyle P(H|G)=\frac{ P(G|H) P(H)}{ P(G)}\) </p>
<p> \(\displaystyle P(H|G)=\frac{ {@prob_A@}({@product_A_1@})}{ {@ta_1@}}\) </p>
<p>\(\displaystyle P(H|G)={@ta_2@}\) </p>

<p>c) \(\displaystyle P(H|G^{\prime})=\frac{ P(G^{\prime}|H) P(H)}{ P(G^{\prime})}\) </p>
<p> \(\displaystyle P(H|G^{\prime})=\frac{ {@1-prob_A@}({@product_A_1@})}{ 1-{@ta_1@}}\) </p>
<p>\(\displaystyle P(H|G^{\prime})={@ta_3@}\) </p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
